 "conclusion": "cc's imageblock addressing bug is the coordinate-register LIFETIME: the store emits its coordinate operand as RELEASE (16) but the register is read again after the store, so every lane collapses to element 0. Fix: emit KEEP (0) when the store coordinate is live-out. D4 reproduces the collapse; D3 refuted the 4-byte y-read hypothesis.",
 "cc_fix_validated": "Piece B's cc fix (liveness-driven slot 6, linker/g17-setb-scalar-receipts) was validated on the M5 Pro: the fresh cc compiles cc_keepcoord_dx0 and cc_keepcoord_dx1 round-trip, BUF2[256+i] = 0xA5000000+i and +(i+1) (lane 31 unscored), 3 runs each -- cc's own imageblock program no longer collapses, retiring item 6's round-trip caveat. The discriminating pair pins it to one bit: cc_release_dx0_control is cc_keepcoord_dx0 with slot 6 flipped keep(0)->release(16), and it collapses BUF2 to 0xA5000000 on all 32 lanes while the keep version varies -- the fix is that one operand in the compiler's own program, not only in Apple's."
